BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:legislature-senate-committee-on-business-and-commerce-20260729T0900@cal
 endars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260827T043204Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260729T110000
SUMMARY:Texas Senate: Business & Commerce - 765-kV lines and grid reliabili
 ty
LOCATION:Room E1.012 (Hearing Room)\, Texas Capitol Extension\, 1100 Congre
 ss Ave.\, Austin\, TX 78701
URL:https://capitol.texas.gov/tlodocs/89R/schedules/html/C5102026072909001.
 HTM
DESCRIPTION:Senate Committee on Business & Commerce\, chaired by Sen. Charl
 es Schwertner. Invited and public testimony on two interim charges:\n\nMan
 aging the Impacts of 765-kV Transmission Lines on Private Property Rights 
 - reviewing the proposed route plans and their effect on homes\, businesse
 s and communities\; whether current regulatory processes and timelines ade
 quately protect landowner rights\; and recommendations for transmission pl
 anning\, permitting and siting.\n\nAssessing the State of the Texas Electr
 ic Grid - SB 6 rulemaking including large load interconnection and transmi
 ssion cost allocation\, ERCOT load forecast confidence\, the Texas Energy 
 Fund and post-Uri reforms\, and whether the ERCOT market remains competiti
 ve.\n\nPublic testimony is limited to 2 minutes per witness. Written testi
 mony needs 15 copies to the committee clerk plus a digital copy by email. 
 Registration closes at 11am on the day of the hearing.\n\nNotice was marke
 d REVISION - check the link for any later change.
CATEGORIES:hearing
X-CAM-ORG:legislature
END:VEVENT
